  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 133 PM MDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\nFriday...Will see an abrupt cutoff to the low and mid level moisture \nsupply as drier air at low and mid levels advects into our counties \nas the dominant ridge over Colorado and southern Wyoming reasserts \nitself. Thus dry and hotter.\n\nSaturday through Wednesday...Isolated to scattered afternoon and \nevening showers and thunderstorms expected, with areal coverage \nincreasing each day due to increased mid level moisture. \nFortunately, more beneficial rains expected concentrated over and \nnear our Snowy, Sierra Madre and Southern Laramie Ranges, with the \nbest chances for convection on Monday through Wednesday. Typical \nweak northwest flow aloft on the northeast periphery of the ridge \naloft will aid in occasional passing shortwave troughs aloft near \npeak heating resulting in increasing convective potential each\nday.",
